## Solution

The **logarithmic residue** of $f(z)$ with respect to a contour $C$ is

$$\frac{1}{2\pi i}\oint_C \frac{f'(z)}{f(z)}\,dz \;=\; N - P,$$

where $N$ = number of zeros and $P$ = number of poles of $f$ inside $C$ (counted with multiplicity).

Here $f(z)=\dfrac{\operatorname{ch} z}{e^{iz}-1}$, with $\operatorname{ch} z = \cosh z = \dfrac{e^z+e^{-z}}{2}$, and $C:|z|=8$.

### Zeros of $f$ (zeros of $\cosh z$ that are not poles)

$\cosh z = 0 \iff e^{2z}=-1 \iff 2z = i(2k+1)\pi \iff z = \dfrac{i(2k+1)\pi}{2},\; k\in\mathbb Z$.

These are simple zeros since $\sinh\!\big(\tfrac{i(2k+1)\pi}{2}\big)=i\sin\!\big(\tfrac{(2k+1)\pi}{2}\big)=\pm i\neq 0$.

We need $|z|<8$, i.e. $\dfrac{(2k+1)\pi}{2}<8$, so $2k+1 < \dfrac{16}{\pi}\approx 5.09$, giving $2k+1\in\{-5,-3,-1,1,3,5\}$:

$$z=\pm\tfrac{i\pi}{2},\;\pm\tfrac{3i\pi}{2},\;\pm\tfrac{5i\pi}{2}\quad (5\pi/2\approx 7.85<8<7\pi/2\approx 11.0).$$

So $N=6$.

### Poles of $f$ (zeros of $e^{iz}-1$)

$e^{iz}-1=0 \iff iz=2k\pi i \iff z=2k\pi,\;k\in\mathbb Z$. These are simple (derivative $ie^{iz}=i\neq 0$), and $\cosh(2k\pi)\neq 0$, so each gives a simple pole.

With $|z|<8$: $z=0,\;\pm 2\pi$ ($2\pi\approx 6.28<8<4\pi\approx 12.57$).

So $P=3$.

### No cancellation

Zeros lie on the imaginary axis ($\operatorname{Re}z=0$); poles lie on the real axis ($\operatorname{Im}z=0$). They never coincide, so no cancellation occurs.

### Result

$$\frac{1}{2\pi i}\oint_{|z|=8}\frac{f'(z)}{f(z)}\,dz = N - P = 6 - 3 = \boxed{3}.$$

